  "name": "Puget Sound Plankton Biomass and Composition Data",
  "description": "Marine EcoSystems Analysis / Puget Sound Environmental Research Program plankton biomass and composition data available through COPEPOD. See the cruise summary web page for a detailed list of cruise dates, number of tows and sampled data. Data can be directly downloaded from the COPEPOD website. Coastal & Oceanic Plankton Ecology, Production & Observation Database (COPEPOD) is an on-line global plankton database by NOAA - National Marine Fisheries Service (NMFS). USER BEWARE: These data are from the corrupted F124 NODC data files.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To provide investigators with an integrated data set of quality-controlled, globally distributed plankton abundance, biomass and composition data, along with co-sampled environmental data.",
